# Camera motion is shared policy; applications translate normalized input to it.
import scene_orbit_types.dl
import scene_framing.dl

to get [UI scene orbit] {a pointer to UI scene orbit:orbit} [is moving]:
    if orbit's duration > 0.0:
        return true
    set yaw to the absolute value of (the UI scene orbit angle of (orbit's desired yaw - orbit's yaw))
    set polar to the absolute value of (orbit's desired polar - orbit's polar)
    set distance to the absolute value of (orbit's desired distance - orbit's distance)
    set target to the length of (orbit's desired target - orbit's camera's target)
    return ((yaw > 0.0000001) or (polar > 0.0000001)) or ((distance > 0.0000001) or (target > 0.0000001))

to [turn UI scene orbit] {a pointer to UI scene orbit:orbit} [by yaw] {floating-point number:yaw} [polar] {floating-point number:polar}:
    require condition ((yaw is finite) and (polar is finite)) reporting "Scene orbit turns require finite angles"
    cancel UI scene orbit focus orbit
    set orbit's desired yaw to the UI scene orbit angle of (orbit's desired yaw + (the UI scene orbit angle of yaw))
    set orbit's desired polar to (orbit's desired polar + polar) clamped between (orbit's minimum polar) and (orbit's maximum polar)

to [zoom UI scene orbit] {a pointer to UI scene orbit:orbit} [by factor] {floating-point number:factor}:
    require condition ((factor is finite) and (factor > 0.0)) reporting "Scene orbit zoom requires a finite positive factor"
    cancel UI scene orbit focus orbit
    set orbit's desired distance to (orbit's desired distance * factor) clamped between (orbit's minimum distance) and (orbit's maximum distance)

to [pan UI scene orbit] {a pointer to UI scene orbit:orbit} [by] {vector:offset}:
    require finite UI scene vector offset
    cancel UI scene orbit focus orbit
    set target to orbit's desired target + (the UI scene vector form of offset)
    require finite UI scene vector target
    set orbit's desired target to target

to [focus UI scene orbit] {a pointer to UI scene orbit:orbit} [on] {vector:target} [viewed from] {vector:eye} [over] {floating-point number:duration} [seconds]:
    require condition ((duration is finite) and (duration >= 0.0)) reporting "Scene focus duration must be finite and nonnegative"
    require finite UI scene vector target
    require finite UI scene vector eye
    set camera to orbit's camera
    set camera's position to the UI scene vector form of eye
    set camera's target to the UI scene vector form of target
    set coordinates to the coordinates of UI scene camera camera in orbit orbit
    set orbit's start yaw to orbit's yaw
    set orbit's start polar to orbit's polar
    set orbit's start distance to orbit's distance
    set orbit's start target to orbit's camera's target
    set orbit's desired yaw to coordinates's yaw
    set orbit's desired polar to coordinates's polar clamped between (orbit's minimum polar) and (orbit's maximum polar)
    set orbit's desired distance to coordinates's distance clamped between (orbit's minimum distance) and (orbit's maximum distance)
    set orbit's desired target to camera's target
    set orbit's duration to duration
    set orbit's elapsed to 0.0
    if duration = 0.0:
        settle UI scene orbit orbit

to get [advance UI scene orbit] {a pointer to UI scene orbit:orbit} [by] {floating-point number:seconds} [seconds]:
    require condition ((seconds is finite) and (seconds >= 0.0)) reporting "Scene orbit time must be finite and nonnegative"
    require condition (0.0 <= orbit's retention < 1.0) reporting "Scene orbit damping retention must be between zero inclusive and one exclusive"
    if ((UI scene orbit orbit is moving) = false) or (seconds = 0.0):
        return false
    if orbit's duration > 0.0:
        set orbit's elapsed to orbit's elapsed + (the minimum of seconds and (orbit's duration - orbit's elapsed))
        set progress to orbit's elapsed / orbit's duration
        set blend to progress * progress * (3.0 - 2.0 * progress)
        set orbit's yaw to the UI scene orbit angle of (orbit's start yaw + (the UI scene orbit angle of (orbit's desired yaw - orbit's start yaw)) * blend)
        set orbit's polar to orbit's start polar + (orbit's desired polar - orbit's start polar) * blend
        set orbit's distance to orbit's start distance + (orbit's desired distance - orbit's start distance) * blend
        set orbit's camera's target to orbit's start target + (orbit's desired target - orbit's start target) * blend
        if progress = 1.0:
            settle UI scene orbit orbit
            return true
    else:
        set blend to 1.0 - (orbit's retention raised to the power of (seconds * 60.0))
        set orbit's yaw to the UI scene orbit angle of (orbit's yaw + (the UI scene orbit angle of (orbit's desired yaw - orbit's yaw)) * blend)
        set orbit's polar to orbit's polar + (orbit's desired polar - orbit's polar) * blend
        set orbit's distance to orbit's distance + (orbit's desired distance - orbit's distance) * blend
        set orbit's camera's target to orbit's camera's target + (orbit's desired target - orbit's camera's target) * blend
        if (UI scene orbit orbit is moving) = false:
            settle UI scene orbit orbit
            return true
    place UI scene orbit orbit
    return true
